program Bug_2_19_OnpageOffpageCaseNoEffect;
// Bug 2.19 (issue 1 of 3 documented under this number; see KNOWN_BUGS.md
// for the other two, noted but not separately exercised here):
// `case <expr> onpage of ...` / `case <expr> offpage of ...` parse without
// error and the forced-page flag is threaded all the way through
// Parser::Case() into the code generator's case dispatch, but the one
// concrete compare-and-jump routine on this target never actually reads
// the flag it's handed; it unconditionally emits the same short-branch
// form regardless of which direction (or neither) was requested. Forcing
// `onpage` vs `offpage` on an otherwise byte-identical `case` should, once
// this bug is fixed, produce two DIFFERENT .asm outputs (a short relative
// branch vs a long jump); today they come out byte-for-byte IDENTICAL,
// confirmed live via a raw diff (this file and its `offpage` baseline
// twin share the same internal program name, so even the emitted
// top-of-file label text matches).
//
// Not separately exercised here (would require its own file/verification
// shape, same "one representative reproduction" rule the suite already
// uses elsewhere - see e.g. 2.37's note): issue 2, `until <cond> onpage;`
// never even parses - confirmed live it fails with "Expected 'END' but
// found 'ONPAGE' Did you forget a semicolon (;) ?", since
// Parser::RepeatUntil() never reads a trailing onpage/offpage token at
// all and the compare-clause parser swallows it as an implicit
// compare-against-0 terminator instead. Issue 3, forcing `onpage` on an
// `if`/`while`/`for` block too large for a short branch has no
// compile-time safety net at all (skips the size measurement the
// automatic path performs) - not reproduced here since it needs a
// deliberately oversized block, not a minimal snippet.
//
// New harness mechanism (see REGRESSION_SUITE_GUIDE.md): <stem>.diffcheck
// names a baseline stem to compile and diff .asm against - FAIL if
// identical (today's bug: forcing either direction has no effect), PASS
// if different.
var
	i : byte;
begin
	i := 1;
	case i onpage of
		0: screen_bg_col := black;
		1: screen_bg_col := white;
	end;
	loop();
end.
